The problem is about coloring a grid graph where edges connect not just adjacent vertices but also diagonals of unit squares. This means that in a grid where each cell can connect to its neighbors (horizontally, vertically, diagonally), we need to ensure no two connected vertices have the same color.

In a grid graph where edges include diagonals, each vertex (i, j) is connected to:
- (i-1, j-1), (i-1, j), (i-1, j+1)
- (i, j-1), (i, j+1)
- (i+1, j-1), (i+1, j), (i+1, j+1)

